[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3635081742","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113752#issuecomment-3635081742","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113752","id":3635081742,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YqvIO","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T02:26:10Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T02:26:10Z","body":"Owh that looks nasty!\n\nYeah the assumption is that when joints are part of the extension, data is supplied. Though we might be ignoring flags around this.\nWe'll need to add something to ensure joints without data are just skipped in updating the skeleton.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3635081742/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3636811574","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113752#issuecomment-3636811574","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113752","id":3636811574,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YxVc2","user":{"login":"recursivenomad","id":128114789,"node_id":"U_kgDOB6LgZQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128114789?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad","html_url":"https://github.com/recursivenomad","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T12:17:21Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T03:21:03Z","body":"Yes, that sounds like a good solution!  And it is worth noting that *partial* data may be supplied by an extension? *(such as orientation data without position data in certain data gloves)* ~~(in this case, only orientation data is missing, as signalled by the `XR_SPACE_LOCATION_ORIENTATION_TRACKED_BIT` being unset, while position data still remains.~~\n\nI also want to emphasize that I think Godot's usage of the `XR_SPACE_LOCATION_ORIENTATION_VALID_BIT` as noted above seems out-of-spec to my OpenXR-novice eye?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3636811574/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3639908216","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113752#issuecomment-3639908216","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113752","id":3639908216,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y9Jd4","user":{"login":"recursivenomad","id":128114789,"node_id":"U_kgDOB6LgZQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128114789?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad","html_url":"https://github.com/recursivenomad","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/recursivenomad/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-11T03:28:33Z","updated_at":"2025-12-13T15:17:50Z","body":"Update: Turns out the metacarpal position data from my runtime extension is bad too, even though they report being valid & tracked.  The Vive implemention seems to superimpose the rotationless metacarpal joints (in gray) on top of the proximal joints 🙄\n\n<img width=\"848\" height=\"635\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6a822b9e-ed20-4c76-a0fd-989874879728\" />\n\nThese axes were generated from the data available in `XRHandTracker.get_hand_joint_transform()`.  I am assuming this is a problem on Vive's end, unless Godot is doing some \"fix-up\" behind the scenes which alters the returned joint transforms.\n\nActually, regarding \"fix-up\" of OpenXR joint data: it seems that the joint axes pictured above do not align with [the OpenXR spec](https://registry.khronos.org/OpenXR/specs/1.1/html/xrspec.html#convention-of-hand-joints).  I assume this is a translation Godot does in order to support skeletal conventions of +Y being the bone roll-axis?\n\nAnyway, for my situation, I am in favour of discarding an **entire** joint's data (without sending it to the world origin) if *either* validity bit is unset for that joint (as any unset validity bit signals that joint is already out-of-spec; at least as I understand it).\n\nI have also raised [a bug report with HTC](https://forum.htc.com/topic/21581-bug-viveopenxrhandtracking-is-not-openxr-compliant-metacarpal-joints/), but I wouldn't hold my breath on it getting addressed anytime soon.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3639908216/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3766150996","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113752#issuecomment-3766150996","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113752","id":3766150996,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7geudU","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-19T02:44:36Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T02:44:36Z","body":"> Actually, regarding \"fix-up\" of OpenXR joint data: it seems that the joint axes pictured above do not align with [the OpenXR spec](https://registry.khronos.org/OpenXR/specs/1.1/html/xrspec.html#convention-of-hand-joints). I assume this is a translation Godot does in order to support skeletal conventions of +Y being the bone roll-axis?\n\nCorrect, OpenXR has a weird 90 degree rotation that doesn't align with a lot of existing assets out in the world, so we re-align them to what seems to be standard.\n\nIt's fun, when you view an asset properly setup for OpenXR in say blender, all the bones stick out instead of being aligned.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3766150996/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3766351072","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113752#issuecomment-3766351072","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113752","id":3766351072,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gffTg","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_